{
  "component": "Date Picker Field",
  "description": "A text field for entering or displaying a date, with a Calendar icon instance inside the input and optional label, description and error text. Ten variants cover five states crossed with a Default or Placeholder value style.\n\nPURPOSE: Provides the form-field half of a date selection pattern. The field shows the chosen date as its value and carries the supporting text around it. The existing description says it is to be paired with the Calendar component, so the field itself holds the trigger and the overlay calendar comes from elsewhere.\n\nBEHAVIOUR: The State property drives Default, Hover, Focus, Error and Disabled appearances. Focus uses the Stroke/Focus Ring and Border/Focus/Default tokens, Error swaps the border and text to the danger tokens and reveals the Error text layer, and Disabled uses the disabled background, border and icon tokens. Value Type switches the value text between a real date (Text/Default/Default) and placeholder wording (Text/Default/Tertiary).\n\nCOMPOSITION: One nested instance, Calendar, sits inside the Input frame as the trigger icon. Child text layers are Label, Description, Value and Error. AI code generators should look for an existing Calendar icon or calendar component in the development codebase before building a new one.\n\nUSAGE: Use for a single date entry in a form. Turn off Has Label only when an external label or table header already names the field. Use Has Description for format hints and Has Error for validation messages. For free text that is not a date, use the standard text input instead.\n\nCODE GENERATION NOTES: Build as a label, input wrapper and message block, with the Error text replacing or sitting below the Description. The error message needs to be linked to the input for assistive technology, and the Disabled state needs the input taken out of the tab order. Hover and Focus are visual states in Figma only, so implement them with CSS pseudo-classes rather than separate variants. The calendar overlay, keyboard date entry, parsing and formatting are not represented in this component set and must be wired to the Calendar component.",
